stem:
A micrograph of a root hair cell from a maize seedling shows these labelled parts:

- **P**: a thick, clearly visible outer boundary, which extends into a long, narrow tube (the root hair);
- **Q**: a thin line lying close against P;
- **R**: a large, clear area that fills most of the cell and reaches into the root hair;
- **S**: one large, rounded body in the thin layer of cytoplasm.
